      "description": "Career Advising | Undergraduate Admissions | Nova Southeastern University Back to Nova Southeastern University Undergraduate Admissions QUICK LINKS Canvas SharkLink Abraham S. Fischler College of Education and School of Criminal Justice Barry and Judy Silverman College of Pharmacy College of Computing, AI, and Cybersecurity College of Dental Medicine College of Optometry College of Psychology Dr. Kiran C. Patel College of Allopathic Medicine Dr. Kiran C. Patel College of Osteopathic Medicine Graduate Admissions H. Wayne Huizenga College of Business and Entrepreneurship Halmos College of Arts and Sciences Ron and Kathy Assaf College of Nursing Shepard Broad College of Law Undergraduate Admissions University School Give Request Info Apply Now Experience The Undergraduate Experience First Time Students International Students Transfer Students Rankings & Reputation Visit Campus Resources for Parents & Families Frequently Asked Questions Upcoming Open House Dates Academics Academics Academics Choosing Your Major Dual Admission Accelerated Admission Programs Premier Programs Experiential Education and Learning (ExEL) Research Opportunities Graduate Programs and Beyond Admissions Admissions Admissions Freshman Applicants Transfer Applicants International Applicants Nursing Applicants Admitted Students Meet the Admissions Team Admissions Ambassadors Funding Funding Your Education Funding Your Education Financial Aid Scholarships Tuition & Fees Net Price Calculator Premier Programs Career Career Preparation Experiential Education Center for Academic and Professional Success Advising Career Development Internships and Shadowing Student Life Student Life Student Life at NSU Living on Campus Dining Options Getting Involved Student Health and Well-being Arts and Culture South Florida Living search box What are you looking for? What are you looking for? Undergraduate Admissions Experience First Time Students International Students Transfer Students Rankings & Reputation Visit Campus Resources for Parents & Families Frequently Asked Questions Upcoming Open House Dates Academics Academics Choosing Your Major Dual Admission Accelerated Admission Programs Premier Programs Experiential Education and Learning (ExEL) Research Opportunities Graduate Programs and Beyond Admissions Admissions Freshman Applicants Transfer Applicants International Applicants Nursing Applicants Admitted Students Meet the Admissions Team Admissions Ambassadors Funding Funding Your Education Financial Aid Scholarships Tuition & Fees Net Price Calculator Premier Programs Career Experiential Education Center for Academic and Professional Success Advising Career Development Internships and Shadowing Student Life Student Life at NSU Living on Campus Dining Options Getting Involved Student Health and Well-being Arts and Culture South Florida Living Quick Links Canvas SharkLink Abraham S. Fischler College of Education and School of Criminal Justice Barry and Judy Silverman College of Pharmacy College of Computing, AI, and Cybersecurity College of Dental Medicine College of Optometry College of Psychology Dr. Kiran C. Patel College of Allopathic Medicine Dr. Kiran C. Patel College of Osteopathic Medicine Graduate Admissions H. Wayne Huizenga College of Business and Entrepreneurship Halmos College of Arts and Sciences Ron and Kathy Assaf College of Nursing Shepard Broad College of Law Undergraduate Admissions University School Give Request Info Apply Now Back to NSU Undergraduate Admissions Academics Career Advising Career Advising Helping You Prepare for the Real World Network smoothly. Diversify your job search strategies. Polish up your cover letter\n                              and résumé. Practice mock interviews. Whether your focus is already laser sharp or\n                              you need a little guidance to thrive, your professional journey will benefit from\n                              the NSU Edge. The career development office at Nova Southeastern University (NSU)\n                              will show you how to get to the top of the food chain in your industry. You’ll become\n                              a confident, capable, and caring professional who can outsmart, outperform, and outlast\n                              your competition. NSU is recognized by the Carnegie Foundation for both Community Engagement and as\n                              a Carnegie Opportunity College. The Community Engagement designation means students\n                              have real opportunities to apply what they learn through community-based projects,\n                              internships, and service. The Opportunity College designation reflects NSU’s success\n                              in helping students from all backgrounds access college and achieve strong career\n                              outcomes and higher earnings. Menu Center for Academic and Professional Success (CAPS) Meet the CAPS Team Career Development Internship and Shadowing Professional Development Undergraduate Advising Overview Advising Glossary Career and Academic Advising Resources FAQ Forms Registering for Classes All 4 Years Dedicated Academic and Career Adviser 180+ Employers Visited the NSU Campus 1,000+ Internships Annually Get the Support and Guidance You Need to Excel One thing you’ll learn about NSU is that we take your success seriously. Your Edge\n                           Adviser will help you build a personalized recruitment plan. Get help writing cover\n                           letters, résumés, and personal statements. Learn how to negotiate your first job offer.\n                           Find jobs, internships, and other opportunities through NSU’s online portal, Handshake . Schedule an Appointment With Your Adviser Internships and Shadowing Give your résumé and portfolio the NSU Edge with internships and shadowing opportunities.\n                           Make the right connections, and get a head start on your career by gaining valuable\n                           skills on the job. Gain Real World Experience Professional Development Time constraints, financial barriers, or lack of access can often get in the way of\n                           career growth. Professional development opportunities, such as trainings and workshops,\n                           will expose you to opportunities you might not have had otherwise. Our career development\n                           office will connect you with grants, workshops, trainings, recruiting events, and\n                           case competitions to enhance your career track. Strengthen Your Professional Skills Case Competitions Case competitions are a chance to network with future employers, earn Experiential\n                           Education and Learning (ExEL) units, and gain hands-on experience. You’ll get together\n                           in teams to solve a case in front of a judging panel composed of senior-level executives\n                           and NSU faculty. It’s also an opportunity to earn coveted internships, job offers,\n                           and scholarships. Learn More Looking for a Job? The Office of Student Employment can help you get more than a paycheck while earning\n                                 your NSU degree. Find out everything you need to know about employment both on and\n                                 off campus. Employment Options for NSU Students Undergraduate Student Outcome Survey Highlights Enter the professional world as a force of nature. Join fellow Sharks in pursuing\n                              advanced degrees and careers across the globe and 30+ states. The sky's the limit\n                              for NSU grads. 75% Used Center for Academic and Professional Success Resources 100% Participated in Experiential Learning 90% Secured Postgraduate Plans Within 6 Months of Graduation 160+ Employers Visited NSU's Main Campus in Person and/or Virtually Employers: Recruit at NSU! Need interns and team members that are fast, sharp, and adaptable? There’s an ocean\n                           of candidates waiting for you here. We’re building a robust pipeline of highly qualified\n                           future employees for you to choose from. We’ve also streamlined recruitment processes\n                           that save you time, money, and organizing headaches. Partner with us to join a roster\n                           of high-profile organizations staffed by our most driven students. Meet Employer Relations You’ll have access to a dedicated team of agile experts to help you organize your\n                           recruitment efforts. Get in Touch This was a great avenue for a virtual event, and the NSU Employer Relations team was\n                                                   very friendly, supportive, and accommodating. HCA Healthcare On-Campus Engagement On-campus events help our Sharks establish fulfilling careers, contribute to society,\n                           and adapt to an ever-changing workplace. Add top-notch candidates to your teams by\n                           participating in our career fairs, information sessions, roundtables, and more. View Events Internships Evaluate future talent by offering students internships within your organization.\n                           Partner with us to hire interns and volunteers. Email CAPS Handshake Our online recruitment portal is free for you to list jobs, internships, and other\n                              opportunities. Students regularly turn to Handshake to find openings. Log In to Handshake Resources for Employers Sample Internship Description Sample Internship Offer Letter Sample Internship Work Schedule Internship Evaluation Form How to Post Jobs and Internships on Handshake Sign up for an account on Handshake . Select the employer account type from the option presented. Fill out the information requested, and then click Sign Up . Once you get to the confirmation page, you’ll get an email with a link to confirm\n                                    your account. Click this link to proceed with the registration process. Create a job description, and post on the Handshake portal. Once a student is selected for an internship, we’ll ask you to provide an offer letter\n                                    to the student outlining the conditions of your offer. Please let us know when you’re signing up so we can look out for your listings! Contact\n                                    the NSU Career Development Office at (954) 262-7201 or email caps@nova.edu to schedule a meeting with a member of the employer relations staff. If you need help with the Handshake process, please contact Niemah Butler at or email niemah@nova.edu . Get Everything You Need for Professional Success Handshake isn’t just an online portal for job listings—it’s also a treasure trove\n                                 of resources you can use to enhance your career. Access: Resume templates Cover letter guides Personal statement guides Interviewing and negotiation strategies for jobs and internships Resources for pre-health students Log In to Handshake Featured Career Development Opportunities Jobs Account Manager, Technology and Lifestyle Services, LCS (Apps Vertical) at Google, Inc. Read More RRT/PSG TECH I 1830-0700 at Cincinnati Children's Read More Radiologic Technologist (Flex Schedule, Variable Shift) $20,250 Bonus at Munson Healthcare Read More CPI Alternative Response Worker Trainee at Texas Department of Family & Protective Services Read More Internships Network Strategy (Capacity Planning) Summer Intern 2027 Read More Engineering Signal Summer Intern 2027 Read More Engineering (Roadway Equipment) Summer Intern 2027 Read More Engineering (Track and Structures) Summer Intern 2027 Read More Events Miami-Dade County Public Schools Connect Cafe, January 8, 2026 (Thursday, January 8th 2026, 4:00 pm - 6:00 pm EST) Read More Citizens Spotlight: Making Sense of Investment Banking (Wednesday, January 21st 2026, 4:00 pm - 5:00 pm EST) Read More Careers in STEM Education: Consulting Beyond the Classroom (Monday, January 26th 2026, 11:00 am PST - Wednesday, January 28th 2026, 12:00 pm PST) Read More Virtual Infosession with Third Bridge! (April 1st) (Wednesday, April 1st 2026, 12:00 pm - 1:00 pm CDT) Read More Career Development User Agreement As a user of this site: I agree to provide accurate and truthful information about my qualifications and educational\n                                    background in my online profile, my résumé, and any supplemental job-search documents\n                                    I upload to the Handshake portal. I will keep my profile information up to date, including my current contact information,\n                                    email address, and academic major and class year. As a current NSU student, I will\n                                    use my @mynsu.nova.edu email address in my profile. I authorize Career Development to release my résumé to employers I have selected via\n                                    Handshake and On-Campus Recruiting (OCR). If participating in OCR, I agree to abide by all OCR policies and procedures. I am responsible for maintaining the confidentiality of my login information and password.\n                                    I am responsible for all uses of my registration, whether or not authorized by me.\n                                    If others use my password to access job listings or to post inappropriate material\n                                    on the site, I risk losing my access to the site. In circumstances in which Career\n                                    Development suspects that account access information has been shared and unauthorized\n                                    access has been granted to the system, I understand the policy is to immediately suspend\n                                    all user privileges, investigate the situation, and possibly refer the case to the\n                                    Office of Student Conduct. Career Development expects NSU students and alumni using Handshake (including for\n                                    on-campus recruiting, job postings, résumé books, and career fair contacts) to honor\n                                    their commitments and think carefully when accepting a job or internship offer. It\n                                    is unprofessional and damaging to both a student’s personal reputation and NSU’s reputation\n                                    as an institution when an individual reneges on an accepted job offer. Please carefully\n                                    consider all options before accepting a position, and if in doubt about whether to\n                                    accept it, consult with a Career Development adviser. Individuals who renege on a\n                                    job or internship offer may face suspension of their Handshake privileges (including\n                                    the on-campus recruiting program). I agree to the Disclaimer and Terms and Conditions. Handshake Terms and Conditions Your use of NSU’s Career Development services and the Handshake portal is deemed to\n                                 constitute your binding agreement to the following terms. If you do not agree to these\n                                 terms, do not use Career Development services or the Handshake portal: The experiential learning, internship, and employment postings on the Handshake portal\n                                 are provided as a convenience to Nova Southeastern University, Inc. (NSU); students\n                                 and alumni (“user(s)”) seeking potential experiential learning, internship, and/or\n                                 employment opportunities; and to businesses, entities, and persons seeking to post\n                                 such opportunities. Use of the Handshake portal and any consequences arising therefrom,\n                                 including but not limited to participation in experiential learning, internship, and/or\n                                 employment opportunities, is solely at the risk of the user. NSU serves as a host for the Handshake portal; however, the businesses, entities,\n                                 and persons seeking interns and/or employees are responsible for fairly and accurately\n                                 reporting the information contained in postings. The experiential learning, internship,\n                                 and/or employment opportunity postings are not created or maintained by NSU, and NSU\n                                 assumes no responsibility for the content of the postings. NSU cannot and does not\n                                 guarantee (a) the truthfulness, completeness, or accuracy of any posting; (b) the\n                                 safety, quality, or academic merit of any experiential learning, internship, or employment\n                                 opportunity; or (c) the credentials of any person or entity posting information. Inclusion\n                                 of any experiential learning opportunity, internship, and/or employment posting on\n                                 the Handshake portal does not constitute and shall not be construed as: An endorsement or approval by NSU; its trustees, officers, or employees; or agents\n                                    of the business, entity, and/or person, nor their business practices; or A warranty or representation by NSU as to the quality, integrity, legitimacy, safety,\n                                    suitability, or other features of such listings, the businesses or entities, and/or\n                                    its owners or agents. Students and alumni using the Handshake portal assume all responsibility to investigate\n                                 and evaluate the content of any postings on the portal, including but not limited\n                                 to the bona fides and suitability of any experiential learning, internship, or employment\n                                 opportunity, as well as the credentials of any individual or entity seeking experiential\n                                 learning students, interns, and/or employees. NSU shall not be liable for any claims,\n                                 demands, causes of action, damage, or injury resulting from, arising out of, or connected\n                                 with the information posted on the Handshake portal or the utilization thereof, including\n                                 but not limited to participation in experiential learning, internship, or employment\n                                 opportunities. By using the Handshake portal, you agree to the terms and conditions stated above. In the event of a dispute between one or more users of the Handshake portal or NSU\n                                 Career Development, you release Career Development and NSU (and our agents and employees)\n                                 from liability for any claims, demands, and damages (actual and consequential, direct\n                                 and indirect, of every kind and nature, known and unknown) arising out of or in any\n                                 way connected with such disputes to the fullest extent permitted by law. If you have questions or concerns about these terms and conditions, please email caps@nova.edu or call (954) 262-7990 . NSU’s Privacy Policy Return to top of page Undergraduate Admissions Apply Now Request Info Call Email Visit Us © Nova Southeastern University 3300 S. University Drive Fort Lauderdale, Florida 33328-2004 Phone: 800-541-6682 Quick Links Default select example Select One... Apply Now Athletics Career Development Current Students Dual Admission Emergency Alert Employment Experiential Education Giving to NSU Graduate Programs Honors Program International Affairs NSU Bookstore Newsroom Office of Financial Assistance Office of the President Request Information Title IX Resources Undergraduate Advising Veterans Resource Center Visit NSU Athletics Experiential Education Graduate Programs Newsroom NSU Bookstore Title IX Resources Visit NSU Career Development Honors Program Giving to NSU Employment Office of Financial Assistance Request Information Apply Now Dual Admission International Affairs Current Students Emergency Alert Office of the President Undergraduate Advising Veterans Resource Center Request A Tour Launch Virtual Tour facebook instagram youtube linkedin Contact Us | Using Our Site | Privacy Policy | GDPR Privacy Notice | ADA Policy | Notice of Nondiscrimination We use cookies and similar technologies to operate and improve our website, analyze website traffic and usage, and support university communications.\nYou can accept all cookies, reject non-essential cookies, or manage your preferences. Privacy Policy | GDPR Policy Accept All Reject Non-Essential Manage Preferences Privacy Preferences Select which types of cookies you allow us to use. You may change your preferences at any time. Essential Cookies Required for site functionality and security. Analytics Cookies Help us understand how visitors use our website (e.g., Google Analytics). Marketing Cookies Used to deliver relevant ads and track campaign performance. Save Preferences ©"
    },
    "https://nsucareers.nova.edu": {
      "title": "Homepage",
      "description": "Homepage Home Search Jobs All Jobs Staff Jobs Faculty Jobs Temporary Jobs Featured Jobs Benefits NSU Culture NSU at a Glance Faculty and Staff News NSU in the News NSU Research NSU Mako Magazine Winter 2025 My Profile Kiosk mode NSU Florida At NSU, we are more than just a workplace—we are a vibrant community. #23 Top Employer in Florida At Nova Southeastern University (NSU), your career is more than just a job—it’s a purpose-driven experience where innovation, growth, and impact come together. As one of Forbes’ Top 25 Employers in Florida, NSU is committed to fostering an environment where employees thrive both professionally and personally. $6 Billion Direct Economic Impact As the largest private research university in Florida, NSU is at the forefront of education, healthcare, and research, with a projected $5 billion economic impact. Our R1 Carnegie Classification places us among the nation’s top-tier research institutions, advancing solutions in cancer treatment, brain health, marine science, and more. 100+ Corporate Partnerships Here at NSU, your growth is our priority. Our commitment to learning and collaboration creates a workplace where you can make a difference—whether you’re shaping future leaders, driving groundbreaking research, or providing essential university services. TAKE YOUR NEXT STEP Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. OR BROWSE BY: All Jobs Faculty Staff Temporary Featured Jobs Faculty & Adjunct Opportunities Faculty / Adjunct Faculty Staff Opportunities Staff Temporary Opportunities Temporary Featured Opportunities Featured Jobs You Belong At NSU At NSU, we believe our team members are our greatest asset, and we’re committed to fostering a supportive workplace where you can thrive. When you join us, you gain access to a comprehensive suite of benefits designed to support your personal and professional journey. Join NSU and be part of a community that values innovation, collaboration, and excellence. Here, you’re not just an employee—you’re a vital part of shaping the future. Employee Health Benefits Explore NSU Health Benefits Retirement Plans Explore Retirement Plans Tuition Waiver Explore Tuition Waiver Health and Wellness Explore Health and Wellness ABOUT FORT LAUDERDALE Fort Lauderdale is a vibrant coastal city in Southeast Florida known for its beautiful beaches, extensive canals, and boating culture. It offers a mix of outdoor recreation, cultural attractions, lively nightlife, and serves as a major cruise port near Miami, making it a key hub in South Florida. Live Live Fort Lauderdale offers a dynamic combination of urban and coastal living, featuring beautiful beaches, a warm climate, and a diverse community. Residents can enjoy outdoor activities such as water sports and boating, along with a vibrant dining and entertainment scene, including cultural events and arts festivals. The city has a variety of neighborhoods to suit different lifestyles, from waterfront homes to urban areas. However, factors like the cost of living, traffic, and hurricane preparedness are important considerations for potential residents. Overall, Fort Lauderdale is an appealing destination for those looking for a sunny and lively lifestyle. NEIGHBORHOODS Davie Fort. Lauderdale Pembroke Pines Sunrise Hollywood Work Work Fort Lauderdale presents a variety of career opportunities in sectors such as tourism, healthcare, maritime, technology, and finance. The tourism industry is particularly significant, driven by the city's appealing beaches and culture, leading to numerous hospitality jobs. The rise of tech startups and growth in the financial sector have also created more roles in IT and finance. The healthcare sector remains robust, with many hospitals and clinics offering employment for medical professionals. Additionally, the city hosts various networking events and career fairs, facilitating connections between job seekers and employers. POPULAR INDUSTRIES IN FORT LAUDERDALE Tourism Healthcare Technology Finance Play Play Fort Lauderdale offers a wide range of recreational activities, including beautiful beaches like Fort Lauderdale Beach, where visitors can swim, sunbathe, and partake in water sports such as jet skiing and paddleboarding. The city's extensive canal system makes it ideal for boating and yachting, providing opportunities for fishing and scenic cruises. For those who prefer land activities, parks like Hugh Taylor Birch State Park offer hiking and biking trails, while the vibrant Las Olas Boulevard features shopping, dining, and art galleries. Additionally, events such as the Fort Lauderdale International Boat Show and various festivals throughout the year enrich the local culture. YEAR-ROUND VACATION FEELING Sports & Recreation Water Sports Arts & Culture Shopping & Dining Learn Learn Fort Lauderdale has become a burgeoning hub for tech innovation, characterized by a vibrant startup ecosystem and a growing number of tech companies. The city benefits from its proximity to major educational institutions, such as Nova Southeastern University, fostering a talent pipeline in areas like marine technology, cybersecurity, and logistics tech. Co-working spaces and incubators, such as the Greater Fort Lauderdale Alliance, support emerging entrepreneurs, while significant investments in infrastructure and a favorable business climate attract established firms. This combination of resources, talent, and investment opportunities positions Fort Lauderdale as an attractive destination for tech innovation. FAST PASS TO SUCCESS Colleges & Universities Elementary, Middle & High Schools NSU Florida - Fort. Lauderdale - Davie Campus America’s Best Colleges 2026 Dr. Harry K. Moon, M.D., FACS, FRCSEd President and Chief Executive Officer Close Candidate Details We use cookies. Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalize, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Quick Links Careers at NSU Your Career, Our Commitment NSU Featured Jobs NSU Employee Benefits Office of Human Resources | NSU NSU at a Glance NSU Office of the President NSU Regional Campuses / Off-Campus Locations Wavelengths NSU Newsroom NSU Research NSU Health | Florida NSU Veterans Resources Notice of Nondiscrimination Employee Rights & Responsibilities Under the Family and Medical Leave Act Notice of Combined Annual Security Report and Annual Fire Safety Report Availability Drug-Free Schools and Campuses Policy Drug and Alcohol-Free Workplace Policy Equal Employment Opportunity: Know Your Rights Child Safety from Sexual Offenders and Predators ©2026 Nova Southeastern University | 3300 S. University Drive, Fort Lauderdale, FL, 33328-2004 | Phone: 800-541-6682 Contact Us | Using Our Site | Privacy Policy | GDPR Privacy Notice | ADA Policy"
    },
