r. Kiran C. Patel College of Allopathic Medicine Dr. Kiran C. Patel College of Osteopathic Medicine Graduate Admissions H. Wayne Huizenga College of Business and Entrepreneurship Halmos College of Arts and Sciences Ron and Kathy Assaf College of Nursing Shepard Broad College of Law Undergraduate Admissions University School Give Request Info Apply Now Back to NSU Center For Academic and Professional Success Find Your Edge Home CAPS It’s a competitive world out there. At Nova Southeastern University, you will learn\n                              how to outsmart, outperform, and outlast the competition. The Center for Academic\n                              and Professional Success (CAPS) is here to help you find your NSU Edge. About CAPS The Center for Academic and Professional Success is exactly what it sounds like: a\n                              destination where you’ll get the tools and support you need to ace your academic life\n                              and your future. Our Vision The Center for Academic and Professional Success (CAPS) at Nova Southeastern University\n                              empowers and supports the holistic development of students as they pursue their academic\n                              and professional goals. Our Mission CAPS collaborates and fosters partnerships with university and external stakeholders\n                              to support students throughout their higher education journey as they become meaningful\n                              contributors in their field. Our goal is to empower students to develop decision-making and self-efficacy, impacting\n                              successful academic program completion and career management. We help students develop\n                              awareness and the ability to take advantage of opportunities that align with and build\n                              on their interests, values, knowledge, and skills. Menu Center For Academic and Professional Success New-Student Information Undergraduate Advising Pre-Health Advising Alumni Resources Employer Engagement Meet the CAPS Team Request a Workshop I have gained skills and experience by writing job descriptions, preparing blog posts\n                                       and visiting the different estates of a business, which will prove to be incredibly\n                                       valuable wherever my future may take me. Madison C.  | Management Services and Resources Your career journey will take you through a continuous cycle of exploration, preparation,\n                                 and action. To gain a competitive advantage, you need a plan. CAPS is here to help\n                                 you design a meaningful career that matches your interests, skills, and values. No\n                                 matter where you are on your journey, NSU has resources to help you stand out. Undergraduate Academic and Career Advising Working with your Career and Academic Success Coach, you will get individualized attention\n                           every step of the way. Your Career and Academic Success Coach will make sure you don’t\n                           miss a beat as you transform from student to working professional, graduate student,\n                           entrepreneur, or whatever your goals are. Through the Center for Academic and Professional Success, you can: Figure out the best major for your dream job. Get help choosing the right courses for your degree. Give your resume and cover letter a professional polish. Practice how to be the best candidate for the job with mock interviews. Access a running database of companies and organizations currently hiring. Use digital career development tools like LinkedIn Learning . Find internships, micro-internships, and shadowing opportunities with local and national\n                              employers that recruit from NSU’s campus. Schedule regular meetings with your adviser or attend a drop-in meeting for urgent\n                           needs. Your success is your Career and Academic Success Coach’s top priority. Schedule an Appointment Connect with More Resources CAPS is a one-stop shop for building your future. Undergraduate Catalog Academic Honor Societies Undergraduate Student Symposium Travel Study Program Undergraduate Student Outcome Survey Highlights Enter the professional world as a force of nature. Join fellow Sharks in pursuing\n                              advanced degrees and careers across the globe and 30+ states. The sky's the limit\n                              for NSU grads. 75% Used Center for Academic and Professional Success Resources 100% Participated in Experiential Learning 90% Secured Postgraduate Plans Within 6 Months of Graduation 160+ Employers Visited NSU's Main Campus in Person and/or Virtually Graduate Student Career Advising Students enrolled in a masters or professional program at Nova Southeastern University\n                           have access to career services offered by the Center for Academic and Professional\n                           Success. These services include help with resume development, interview preparation,\n                           job search assistance, and occupational exploration and transition. Schedule an Appointment Graduate students at NSU have access to Handshake. Log Into Handshake How to Schedule an Appointment in Navigate Step 1: Select \"Schedule an Appointment\" Step 2: Follow the prompts, then select the appointment type that you are seeking Step 3: Select where you would like the appointment and with which adviser Step 4: Pick a time that works for you and confirm appointment Alumni Resources Alumni who have a conferred degree from NSU have access to career services offered\n                           by CAPS. These services include help with résumé development, interview preparation,\n                           job search assistance, applying to graduate/professional school and occupational exploration\n                           and transition. While services are provided to assist alumni in managing their job\n                           search efforts, they are not to be viewed as a placement service. As an alumnus of NSU, you get access to Handshake. Log Into Handshake Unlock Your Potential With Our Help Launch Virtual Tour Featured Career Opportunities Events Social Determinants of Mental Health Case Competition  (Tuesday, February 6th 2024, 12:00 am EST - Tuesday, March 19th 2024, 12:00 am EDT) Read More NSU Clinical Psychology Case Competition (Tuesday, February 6th 2024, 12:00 am EST - Tuesday, March 19th 2024, 12:00 am EDT) Read More Neuroscience- Pluripotent Stem Cells Case Competition (Tuesday, February 6th 2024, 12:00 am EST - Tuesday, March 19th 2024, 12:00 am EDT) Read More Marine & Environmental Science Case Competition (Tuesday, February 6th 2024, 12:00 am EST - Tuesday, March 19th 2024, 12:00 am EDT) Read More Jobs Account Manager, Technology and Lifestyle Services, LCS (Apps Vertical) at Google, Inc. Read More RRT/PSG TECH I 1830-0700 at Cincinnati Children's Read More Radiologic Technologist (Flex Schedule, Variable Shift) $20,250 Bonus at Munson Healthcare Read More CPI Alternative Response Worker Trainee at Texas Department of Family & Protective Services Read More Internships Network Strategy (Capacity Planning) Summer Intern 2027 Read More Engineering Signal Summer Intern 2027 Read More Engineering (Roadway Equipment) Summer Intern 2027 Read More Engineering (Track and Structures) Summer Intern 2027 Read More Contact Information Ready to dive in? We’re here to help! I f you have any questions, please email the Center for Academic and Professional Success at caps@nova.edu or call (954) 262-7990 . Appointments Current Students : Log in to Navigate Alumni : Call (954) 262-7990 Hours Monday–Friday: 8:30 a.m.–5:00 p.m. EST Dual Admission Career and Academic Advising Office Hours Wednesday and Friday 9:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. via Phone or In-person Undergraduate Career and Academic Advising Drop-in Hours Monday and Thursday 11:00 a.m. - 2:00 p.m. via Phone or In-person Contact Us Email Call Us Apply Now Request Info Return to top of page © Nova Southeastern University 3300 S. University Drive Fort Lauderdale, FL  33328-2004 Phone: 800-541-6682 Quick Links Default select example Select One... Apply Now Athletics Canvas Career Development Current Students EASE Grant Performance Emergency Alert Employment Faculty and Staff Resources Giving to NSU Human Resources International Affairs Map of Campus NSU Bookstore NSU Health NSU Libraries Newsroom Office of Financial Aid Office of the President Request Information Sharklink Title IX Resources University School Veterans Resource Center Visit NSU Apply Now Athletics NSU Bookstore Canvas Career Development Current Students Emergency Alert Employment EASE Grant Performance Faculty and Staff Resources Office of Financial Aid Giving to NSU NSU Health Human Resources International Affairs NSU Libraries Map of Campus Newsroom Office of the President Request Information Sharklink Title IX Resources University School Veterans Resource Center Visit NSU Request A Tour Launch Virtual Tour facebook instagram youtube linkedin Contact Us | Using Our Site | Privacy Policy | GDPR Privacy Notice | ADA Policy | Notice of Nondiscrimination We use cookies and similar technologies to operate and improve our website, analyze website traffic and usage, and support university communications.\nYou can accept all cookies, reject non-essential cookies, or manage your preferences. Privacy Policy | GDPR Policy Accept All Reject Non-Essential Manage Preferences Privacy Preferences Select which types of cookies you allow us to use. You may change your preferences at any time. Essential Cookies Required for site functionality and security. Analytics Cookies Help us understand how visitors use our website (e.g., Google Analytics). Marketing Cookies Used to deliver rele